From: wangzlei <66336933+wangzlei@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 05:43:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] aws-red-attrs: AWS resource attributes on HTTP client RED
 metrics

Upstream's S3/SQS parsers (and patch 07's Lambda parser) enrich spans only; the
HTTP client RED metrics of an AWS SDK call carry just server.address, so a
dashboard cannot tell which bucket, queue or function a service talks to.

This patch adds them as default attributes of the HTTP client metric group
(http.client.request.duration, http.client.request.body.size,
http.client.response.body.size), the same mechanism patch 03 uses for
peer.service.name:
- aws.s3.bucket (semconv)         S3 calls with a bucket
- aws.sqs.queue.url (semconv)     SQS calls whose payload names the queue
- aws.lambda.function.arn         Lambda Invoke, unqualified ARN
- faas.invoked_name / faas.invoked_region (semconv)  Lambda Invoke

aws.lambda.function.arn: no semconv attribute covers the client side
(aws.lambda.invoked_arn is the server-side ARN as given to the function,
qualifier included), so the name follows the AWS SDK instrumentation used by
ADOT / Application Signals. It is the unqualified ARN, so calls to the same
function by name, ARN or ARN:alias share one series. The Lambda parser sets it
when the call names the account: a full ARN is kept up to the function name;
a partial ARN (<account>:function:<name>) is completed with the endpoint region
and its partition (aws / aws-cn / aws-us-gov). A call by bare name targets the
caller's account, which OBI does not know: the ARN is left out and the
collector completes it from cloud.account.id (adot-obi config/otel.yaml,
transform/aws). The ARN is also added to the Lambda span.

The getters return an invalid KeyValue for every span the AWS parsers did not
recognize (and for S3 / SQS calls without bucket / queue), so the OTEL
exporter's Expirer drops them: plain HTTP client datapoints keep exactly their
upstream attribute set. aws.s3.bucket / aws.sqs.queue.url getters used to emit
an empty string for such spans (they were not default metric attributes).
Prometheus label sets are fixed, so there the omitted value is "".

SQS parser: a body rebuilt from the captured buffer that ends before its
Content-Length (seen for Go clients, whose SQS response body is often not in the
capture) no longer fails the whole parse; the captured part is used. Before,
Go aws-sdk-go-v2 SQS calls were never parsed; now ReceiveMessage is (SendMessage
mostly still lacks a captured response, an upstream Go large-buffer limit).

Cardinality: one series per bucket / queue / function an application calls;
no request data (object key, message id, qualifier) is used. Documented in
devdocs/metrics.md.

Why upstream does not do it: upstream only enriches the spans.

Turn it off: attributes.select exclude per metric, or drop this patch.

Adot-Obi-Patch: 08-aws-red-attrs
